# ARGIA Pi crontab — the Pi is the OFF-SITE vantage point since the
# 2026-08-26 decommission: it runs nothing that pio06 runs. Edit with
# `crontab -e`; NEVER run `crontab <file>` (it replaces the whole table).
#
# v217.1 (2026-09-06 check-up): every job must run FROM THE REPO CHECKOUT
# (~/argia_v2) so deploy.sh keeps it current. A copy in ~/report_watch
# probed report.argia.com.mx for two days after the portal switch and
# pushed a false "DOWN" every hour.
#
# Pi system timezone: America/Mexico_City (check: timedatectl).
# Scripts are called through `bash`: Git for Windows does not record the
# executable bit, so the mode in the checkout cannot be relied on.

# deploy: follow origin/main (every 10 min; does nothing unless main moved)
*/10 * * * * bash /home/zemel/argia_v2/v2/pi/deploy.sh >> /home/zemel/argia_logs/deploy_cron.log 2>&1

# portal watchdog — is https://portal.argia.com.mx/login answering? ntfy on DOWN/UP
*/5 * * * * bash /home/zemel/argia_v2/v2/pi/report_watch/report_watch.sh >> /home/zemel/argia_logs/report_watch.log 2>&1

# outage-mode PPA watch — only acts while the server is down (daylight)
*/30 8-19 * * * bash /home/zemel/argia_v2/v2/pi/report_watch/ppa_watch.sh >> /home/zemel/argia_logs/ppa_watch.log 2>&1

# off-site backups — nightly pull of the DB dump, auth DB, portfolio snapshot, report PDFs
0 22 * * * bash /home/zemel/argia_v2/v2/pi/db_backups/pull_backup.sh >> /home/zemel/argia_logs/db_backup_pull.log 2>&1

# CFE tariff fetcher (its own tree in ~/cfe — see pi/cfe/README.md)
10 8 * * * /home/zemel/cfe/cfe_daily.sh

# log hygiene — SD cards die of log diarrhea
17 3 * * * find /home/zemel/argia_logs -name '*.log' -size +5M -exec truncate -s 1M {} \;
